    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Hoederer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "—"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "What these shadows tell of is the second Kazdel that could be called a city."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "After the very first Kazdel was laid to waste by the Elders and Ancients, there passed over a thousand years where Kazdel was no more than a tiny hamlet, a mass of thatch and wooden fencing."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Frail, easily destroyed, it was ravaged by the wills of colonizers again and again, and again and again the Sarkaz were sent into exile."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Until this moment, where the Sarkaz had once again accumulated strength, once again rebuilt... a true city."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "They left the wastes that we now call Columbia, and came to the heartlands of Terra, and there they lived, and there they died."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "And then... a betrayal. Another migration east. And before they'd gone far, the blue flames of fury were again betrayed."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "It seems as if Sarkaz history were cursed from that moment on."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "History's waves have rolled on, to this present day, where citadels are incessantly scrapped and rebuilt and still amble about in arm's reach."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "???",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "But the names they speak, those are that city's first Kings of Sarkaz."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "The Kings of Sarkaz, seven thousand years ago."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "How—"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "How did you produce these things?"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Hoederer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "......"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Considering this Kazdel's historical significance and its impact on the generations to come, the legend of the Kings of Sarkaz have found such wide spread in song."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "But these vagabonds? Even we lack for such trifling... er, accounts."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "This is scarcely even witchcraft... it is absolutely not. No Originium Arts could attain this degree of effect. Oh, or perhaps it could, but at the very least a historian would be needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Is it a trick of physics? A projector that forms images from the mist? When did our brother and sister gain such technology? How rude not to share!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Hm... no, it's off. These pictures are too close to the <i>recorded</i> truth. Be it a technological feat, whence came the material...?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "So this is some kind of Arts, then..."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "But it's of no known category of Arts... it's highly likely, even, that it isn't Arts."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "How very strange—a Feranmut? If Victoria wanted to tame a Feranmut for battle, it should've started long ago..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "W",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "What's this bitch even doing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "It seems you are not Artists."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Ermengarde",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "You are simply and purely the ones who blew up my beloved cube. It was very comfortable sitting in it."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Hoederer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Messenger to the Lich's Court, Lady Ermengarde, we deeply apologize for using such a method to contact you."
